From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 16:38:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] cpuidle: apple: Add T8132

The T8132 (M4) behaves like the T6040: iBoot locks CYC_OVRD, so the
CPU PD state cannot run, and a plain WFI already powers an idle core
down (the arm64 idle code saves the registers it loses). Run both
entries through WFI when the device tree has an "apple,t8132-cpuidle"
node, as for "apple,t6041-cpuidle".

Without a cpuidle driver, suspend-to-idle never reaches
cpuidle_enter_s2idle(), so the tick is never frozen and timekeeping is
never suspended. Normal idle does not change: it is already WFI.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
(cherry picked from commit 552af4315e23d9a60f8d78d5b027b8089414da81)
---
 drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-apple.c | 16 ++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-apple.c b/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-apple.c
index 7a53c01792..896b92440e 100644
--- a/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-apple.c
+++ b/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-apple.c
@@ -124,16 +124,19 @@ static struct cpuidle_driver apple_idle_driver = {
 
 static int apple_cpuidle_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
-	bool t604x = of_device_is_compatible(pdev->dev.of_node, "apple,t6041-cpuidle");
+	struct device_node *np = pdev->dev.of_node;
+	bool wfi_only = of_device_is_compatible(np, "apple,t6041-cpuidle") ||
+			of_device_is_compatible(np, "apple,t8132-cpuidle");
 
 	/*
 	 * CPU PD writes CYC_OVRD, which is an undefined instruction on
-	 * T8140. Its WFI already lets the hardware power-gate idle
-	 * secondary cores, so both entries must use WFI. Keep index 1:
-	 * the generic s2idle selector skips fallback index 0, otherwise
-	 * tick_freeze() and timekeeping suspension are never reached.
+	 * T8140 and the M4 SoCs (T6041, T8132). Their WFI already lets
+	 * the hardware power-gate idle cores, so both entries must use
+	 * WFI. Keep index 1: the generic s2idle selector skips fallback
+	 * index 0, otherwise tick_freeze() and timekeeping suspension are
+	 * never reached.
 	 */
-	if (of_machine_is_compatible("apple,t8140") || t604x)
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("apple,t8140") || wfi_only)
 		apple_idle_driver.states[STATE_PWRDOWN] = apple_idle_driver.states[STATE_WFI];
 
 	return cpuidle_register(&apple_idle_driver, NULL);
@@ -141,6 +144,7 @@ static int apple_cpuidle_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 static const struct of_device_id apple_cpuidle_of_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "apple,t6041-cpuidle" },
+	{ .compatible = "apple,t8132-cpuidle" },
 	{ .compatible = "apple,t8140-cpuidle" },
 	{ }
 };
